  "id": "relative-pitch",
  "term": "relative pitch",
  "definition": "Relative pitch is the ability to understand or identify musical notes by their relationship to a tonal center, especially the intervals they form with the keynote or tonic. In contrast to absolute pitch, it depends on context-based comparison rather than treating each heard note as a fixed label.",
